<title>USA: Boeing, Delta in supply talks - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Boeing, Delta in supply talks - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co is negotiating with Delta Air Lines Inc to obtain an exclusive supply agreement, the Wall Street Journal said in its electronic edition Tuesday.</p>
<p>The report said the pact would be similar to the one Boeing reached with AMR's American Airlines and would have Delta buy all its future jetliners exclusively from Boeing at guaranteed prices.</p>
<p>The report said people familiar with the discussions also believe Delta could choose either a limited firm order or Boeing's offer for a longer-term arrangment possibly involving billions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
